{
  "_doc": [
    "The Data fields a layout DECLARES — data[] items, after the layout's styles and includes are expanded — per platform, as [name, class as written in the layout].",
    "Read by shared/core/layout_data_fields.py (the collector validate uses to check initialState keys and values; test_tools/tests/test_layout_data_fields_vectors.py runs it) and by each generator's spec (sjui / kjui / rjui), which run the generator's own expansion and extraction on the same files: the four must agree, case by case.",
    "Only declared data counts (plan test-runner-initialstate-and-related, decision 1). Fields a generator adds by itself are listed as absent on purpose (generated_fields_are_not_declared).",
    "files: paths under the project source, layouts/<name>.json and styles/<name>.json. screen: the layout whose fields are listed."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "flat_root_data",
      "why": "Every data[] item of the root, in order, with the class as written (closures included: they are declared).",
      "files": {
        "layouts/screen.json": {
          "type": "View",
          "data": [
            {
              "name": "title",
              "class": "String"
            },
            {
              "name": "count",
              "class": "Int"
            },
            {
              "name": "isOn",
              "class": "Bool"
            },
            {
              "name": "note",
              "class": "String?"
            },
            {
              "name": "onTap",
              "class": "() -> Void"
            }
          ],
          "child": []
        }
      },
      "screen": "screen",
      "expected": {
        "ios": [
          [
            "title",
            "String"
          ],
          [
            "count",
            "Int"
          ],
          [
            "isOn",
            "Bool"
          ],
          [
            "note",
            "String?"
          ],
          [
            "onTap",
            "() -> Void"
          ]
        ],
        "android": [
          [
            "title",
            "String"
          ],
          [
            "count",
            "Int"
          ],
          [
            "isOn",
            "Bool"
          ],
          [
            "note",
            "String?"
          ],
          [
            "onTap",
            "() -> Void"
          ]
        ],
        "web": [
          [
            "title",
            "String"
          ],
          [
            "count",
            "Int"
          ],
          [
            "isOn",
            "Bool"
          ],
          [
            "note",
            "String?"
          ],
          [
            "onTap",
            "() -> Void"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "data_on_a_node_with_other_keys",
      "why": "A data[] on a non-root node that also has other keys: sjui / kjui read data at any level; rjui reads it only on the root, an include root, or a node whose keys are data (and type).",
      "files": {
        "layouts/screen.json": {
          "type": "View",
          "data": [
            {
              "name": "a",
              "class": "String"
            }
          ],
          "child": [
            {
              "type": "View",
              "id": "box",
              "data": [
                {
                  "name": "b",
                  "class": "Int"
                }
              ],
              "child": []
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "screen": "screen",
      "expected": {
        "ios": [
          [
            "a",
            "String"
          ],
          [
            "b",
            "Int"
          ]
        ],
        "android": [
          [
            "a",
            "String"
          ],
          [
            "b",
            "Int"
          ]
        ],
        "web": [
          [
            "a",
            "String"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
